<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Runder Berg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Runder Berg is a hill near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-urach">Bad Urach</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, the site of a fortified Alemannic hilltop settlement of the 4th and 5th centuries. Excavations from 1967 found evidence of an elite residence, metalworking and fine jewellery production. It is one of the best-studied Alemannic hill sites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/runder-berg.jpg" alt="Runder Berg" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ustill · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Runder_Berg.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
